<newsitem itemid="156028" id="root" date="1996-10-31" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: INTRUST HALF YEAR SHARE, DIVIDEND RISE.</title>
<headline>INTRUST HALF YEAR SHARE, DIVIDEND RISE.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     9.24	  vs 8.40</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 9.00	  vs 8.00 </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   7.82	  vs 7.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   7.96	  vs 7.14</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.14	  vs 0.04</p>
<p>Div payable November 29</p>
<p>on register November 15</p>
<p>Full name: Invest Investment Trust Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Intrust said it planned to continue its policy of</p>
<p>issuing its shares in exchange for selected appropriate</p>
<p>shareholdings in order to expand its portfolio and enhance its</p>
<p>stock's tradeability.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
